---
import SectionHeader from './SectionHeader.astro';
---

<!-- Draft copy; final text in issue #5 -->
<section id="problem" class="section" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="container problem">
    <SectionHeader
      eyebrow="The problem"
      title="The fire record is split in two"
      headingId="problem-title"
    />
    <div class="prose problem-body">
      <p>
        Satellites have been spotting fires from orbit for more than twenty years. But that record
        comes from two different instruments, MODIS and VIIRS, which see the ground at very different
        resolutions.
      </p>
      <p>
        Put their hotspot counts side by side and the line jumps in 2012, the year VIIRS arrived. Fires
        didn’t suddenly multiply. The sensor changed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Without one consistent record, responders, land managers and scientists can’t tell whether a
        season is truly unusual or just measured differently.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem-body {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .problem {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr;
      gap: var(--space-2xl);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>
